  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180841/rss" title="webkit.org" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;Announcing &lt;em&gt;Interop 2026&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180842/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Interop project&lt;/a&gt; forms the basis for Google, Apple, Igalia, Microsoft, and Mozilla to collaborate each year on implementing the web technology that developers most want and need. This year sees &lt;em&gt;fifteen&lt;/em&gt; brand new topics, including improvements to &lt;code&gt;attr()&lt;/code&gt;, container style queries, &lt;code&gt;contrast-color()&lt;/code&gt;, scroll-driven animations, and tightening up the CSS Scroll Snap spec.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Wu and Simmons (WebKit) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

