&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🥳 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180848/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Chrome 145 has been released&lt;/a&gt; with support for &lt;code&gt;column-wrap&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;column-height&lt;/code&gt; properties – &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180849/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;demos and explanations here.&lt;/a&gt; The DevTools have &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180850/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;also seen some enhancements.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🕹️ Not content to merely &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180851/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;port Quake to run in the browser&lt;/a&gt;, the creator of Three.js now has &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180852/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;a &lt;em&gt;Descent&lt;/em&gt; port too&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180853/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;source&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;✋ The EU wants &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180854/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;to tackle 'addictive UI' patterns&lt;/a&gt; like infinite scrolling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤖 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180855/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Google shows off a preview of WebMCP&lt;/a&gt;, a proposed standard for sites to offer up abilities to AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤖 Cloudflare is rolling out &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180856/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;a feature to allow agents to fetch Markdown directly&lt;/a&gt; from Cloudflare-powered sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📄 The CSSWG has published a first &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/180857/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;public working draft of Selectors Level 5.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
